From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:12:53 +0900
Subject: Keys and candidates: accessible buttons with stable identifiers

Screen readers and UI tests could not find the keyboard's keys: key panels and candidate delegates
are plain items, and the icon-only keys (Shift, Backspace, Space, language) have no text at all.
Each key panel is now an accessible button named by what it types or does, with an identifier that
stays the same in every interface language (key:<text>, shift, backspace, space, enter, language,
symbol, mode, hide, handwriting; candidate, alternate; language:<locale> in the language popup).
Passive only: no accessible action is added, a key is still pressed by touching it.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-07
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [accessibility; to submit to KDE after the round-3 acceptance]
X-Rungic-Tests: acceptance checklist E2E-02 (docs/121, agent-driven on the phone)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/41
